    'media-advertising' => [
        'what_they_do' => 'Oman\'s media/advertising space includes newspapers (Oman Observer, Times of Oman, Muscat Daily, Al Roya, Al Watan, Oman Arabic), magazines (OER, Oman Economic Review, Business Today, y Magazine), agencies (Ithraa-linked communications, Mindshare Oman, MullenLowe, Gulf Hill & Knowlton), production houses, photographers, videographers, and a fast-growing influencer/creator economy on Instagram and TikTok.',
        'team_reality' => 'Account execs at agencies chase pitches with Omantel, Ooredoo, Bank Muscat, and ministries, weekly creative reviews, monthly campaign launches. Journalists cover events at OCEC, ministries, and embassies. Influencers handle brand deals DM-first and meet clients at Kaffa Café or Crowne Plaza lobby. Media sales teams at newspapers pitch advertisers block by block. Industry meetups happen at Oman Marketing Awards, Dubai Lynx, and regional PR forums.',
        'cardify_fit' => 'Creators and influencers are Cardify\'s perfect user, a QR card that auto-saves into a brand manager\'s phone with IG/TikTok/YouTube links AND a media-kit PDF is exactly what the industry needs. For agency account execs, Cardify digital cards track which client meetings produce follow-ups (analytics). Printed cards still matter for the editor-in-chief meetings and ministry PR officer introductions. Bilingual EN/AR matches Oman media\'s dual-market reality.',
        'use_cases' => [
            'QR cards with IG/TikTok/media-kit links for creators and influencers',
            'Analytics-tracked cards for agency AEs managing 10+ client pitches',
            'Printed cards for editor-in-chief and ministry PR introductions',
        ],
    ],

    'professional-services' => [
        'what_they_do' => 'Oman\'s professional services sector covers the Big 4 (PwC, Deloitte, KPMG, EY), mid-tier audit firms (Moore Stephens, Crowe Oman, BDO, Grant Thornton), law firms (Said Al Shahry, AMJ, Curtis Mallet-Prevost, Trowers & Hamlins), management consultants, tax advisors, ICV consultancies, HR consultancies, and thousands of sole-practitioner CRs doing bookkeeping, PRO services, and company formation across Muscat and Salalah.',
        'team_reality' => 'Audit seniors live at client sites during Feb–May year-end season; tax partners fly to Dubai and London constantly. Lawyers run back-to-back Ministry of Commerce, ROP, and court appearances. Consultants attend Oman CEO Conference, IIA Oman, ICAO Oman, and the annual ITHCA-hosted investor days. PRO services reps race between MoL, MoCIIP, and municipality counters all morning.',
        'cardify_fit' => 'A Big 4 audit senior meeting 15 client contacts in a week benefits hugely from QR, one scan saves full contact + LinkedIn + client-engagement page. For law-firm partners in front of ministry officials, a printed card with OSGA bar registration and ISO 9001 badges still signals formality. Cardify team templates enforce Big 4 brand compliance across 80+ consultants. Central control prevents rogue partners printing unauthorised variants.',
        'use_cases' => [
            'QR cards for Big 4 audit seniors doing 15+ client touchpoints weekly',
            'Printed cards with OSGA bar registration for lawyers in court/ministry',
            'Central brand enforcement across 80+ Big 4 consultants in Oman',
        ],
    ],

    'government-defense' => [
        'what_they_do' => 'Oman\'s government sector spans the Diwan of Royal Court, Royal Oman Police (ROP), Ministry of Defence (MoD), Royal Army of Oman (RAO), Royal Air Force of Oman (RAFO), Royal Navy of Oman, Internal Security Service, plus the civilian ministries (MoCIIP, MoTCIT, MoH, MoE, MoHERI, MoF, etc.) and e-government units like Information Technology Authority (now under MoTCIT) and Tanfeedh.',
        'team_reality' => 'Ministry officials host vendor meetings in formal ministry lobbies with strict security and formal dress code. Defence and security procurement is via long RFP cycles with paper-heavy documentation. Officials attend Oman Defence Exhibition (ODEX), IDEX Abu Dhabi, and OCEC-hosted policy dialogues. Civil-service officers often have double duties across ministries, networking at Diwan-hosted national days and OCCI (Oman Chamber) committees.',
        'cardify_fit' => 'Government is the most formal customer, printed cards with Arabic first, ISO badges, and ministry-approved colour palettes are expected. Cardify\'s bilingual EN/AR templates and central brand control suit this perfectly. Digital QR cards layer on for trade-show scenarios at ODEX and IDEX. Bulk ordering supports department-level rollouts (e.g., 200 cards for a newly appointed department head and their team in one order). Analytics stay private and discreet.',
        'use_cases' => [
            'Bilingual EN/AR printed cards meeting strict ministry formality',
            'Bulk departmental orders for ministry teams and RAFO/RAO units',
            'QR cards for officials representing Oman at ODEX and IDEX Abu Dhabi',
        ],
    ],

    'conglomerate' => [
        'what_they_do' => 'Oman\'s family conglomerates are foundational: Zubair Corporation, Suhail Bahwan Group, Khimji Ramdas, OTE Group, Mohsin Haider Darwish (MHD), Omar Zawawi Establishment (OMZEST), Al Taher Group, Jawad Sultan Group, W.J. Towell, and Bahwan Engineering Group. Each spans multiple sectors, automotive, trading, construction, F&B, banking, real estate, ICT, often with 20–40 operating companies under one family office.',
        'team_reality' => 'Group CEOs and family principals hold weekly council meetings at family offices in Al Khuwair, Qurum, or Bausher. Division MDs run their verticals semi-independently but meet principals quarterly. Group BD attends every major Oman event, OCEC, OIF, OGWA, Oman Design & Build Week, Oman Sustainability Week, Cityscape. Cross-division business happens inside the group, one unit referring a client to another is the lifeblood.',
        'cardify_fit' => 'Group-level brand consistency is the single hardest thing for a conglomerate, Cardify\'s central brand control and per-division template variations solve exactly this. Digital cards can link to the parent-group website + the specific subsidiary landing page, showing visitors the full portfolio in one scan. Printed cards remain essential at principal-level meetings. Bulk ordering covers 500+ employees across 20+ subsidiaries in one order, with division-level logo variants automatically applied.',
        'use_cases' => [
            'Central brand control across 20+ subsidiaries with division variants',
            'QR cards linking to parent-group + subsidiary landing pages',
            'Bulk orders of 500+ cards spanning all operating companies',
        ],
    ],

    'other' => [
        'what_they_do' => 'Small and medium enterprises (SMEs) make up the bulk of Oman\'s business population, supported by Riyada (Authority for SME Development), Sharakah, Oman Technology Fund, and bank SME lending programs. These firms span crafts, home businesses, freelance consultants, micro-factories, specialty retailers, and new concepts that don\'t fit neatly into standard sector classifications. Many operate out of Madayn incubators or home offices across all 11 wilayats.',
        'team_reality' => 'Founders wear every hat, sales, ops, delivery, finance. They meet clients at Kaffa, Slider Station, Crowne Plaza lobby, or directly at client premises. Networking happens at Riyada events, Madayn SME Gate activations, Ithraa export-readiness workshops, OCCI SME committees, and informal WhatsApp groups. Many rely 100% on WhatsApp and Instagram for lead generation, paper cards are often an afterthought.',
        'cardify_fit' => 'Cardify was built for exactly this segment. A single founder who meets 20 prospects a month needs a QR card that saves contact + Instagram + WhatsApp + website in one scan, no reprints, no cost per lead. Bilingual EN/AR handles Oman\'s dual-market reality. When the business grows to 5 staff, team templates and bulk ordering scale smoothly. Analytics show which networking event actually produced leads, invaluable for a resource-tight SME.',
        'use_cases' => [
            'Founder-friendly QR cards with IG, WhatsApp, and website links',
            'Bilingual EN/AR templates for mixed-language Omani clients',
            'Scale-up path from 1 founder to 5-person team with consistent branding',
        ],
    ],

